{"continuation_of":null,"footnotes":[{"marker":"2","text":"Maximum Spectacle Blind size shall be 12NPS. A blind and spacer shall be used for larger pipe sizes. Spectacle Blind material shall be A516 Gr 70N. For low temperature service, material shall be Charpy Y-notch tested at temperatures no warmer than the minimum allowable operating temperature."},{"marker":"4","text":"See Owner's Specification GS 2.10 for Nondestructive Examination requirements. When the amount of radiographic examination is less than 100%, the progressive examination requirements of B31.3 Clause 341.3.4 or CSA Z662 Clause 7.10.3.1 shall apply."},{"marker":"5","text":"Maximum allowable temperature 100°C."},{"marker":"16","text":"For glycol and hot oil service, use SW fittings, except valves which may be threaded."},{"marker":"18","text":"A53 Gr. B Pipe may be substituted with approval. (ERW for NPS 12-18, DSAW for NPS 20-24). Check wall thickness."},{"marker":"24","text":"If using SW flanges, bore to match pipe."},{"marker":"26","text":"For FF Flanges use Class 150 - 3 mm THK Full Face Gaskets, \"Klinger® 1000\", \"Durlon-8600\" or \"Garlock 3150\"."},{"marker":"28","text":"RFSO flanges may be substituted with approval."},{"marker":"29","text":"For treated de-ironized boiler feed water upstream of the deaerator, use 304L stainless steel pipe and fittings with 316 stainless steel valves."},{"marker":"31","text":"Use Flat Faced (FF) flanges in firewater service or when mating to cast iron flanges."}],"header_rows":1,"rows":[{"cells":[{"is_header":true,"value":"CODE B31.3"},{"is_header":true,"value":"CLASS A0"}]},{"cells":[{"type":"text","value":"Service"},{"type":"text","value":"Sweet Gas and Hydrocarbon Liquids, Glycol, Fuel Gas, Propane, Refrigerant, BFW (Note 20), Steam, Steam Cond., Pressure Relief, H.C. Drains, Lube Oil (Pickled.), Fire Water Per ANSI B16.5 Class 150 Material Group 1.1"}]},{"cells":[{"type":"text","value":"Temperature Range"},{"type":"text","value":"-29°C to 204°C"}]},{"cell